            <ArticleTitle>Primary extra-axial, para-articular Chordoma of the knee. A case report and the review of literaturę.</ArticleTitle>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1111/his.13440</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Chordoma is a rare malignant tumor demonstrating notochordal differentiation [1]. It almost invariably arises in the axial skeleton however rare examples of primary extra-axial chordomas have been reported [2-5]. We describe herein, for the first time, a primary conventional chordoma arising in the synovium of the knee joint. This article is protected by copyright. All rights reserved.</AbstractText>
                <CopyrightInformation>This article is protected by copyright. All rights reserved.</CopyrightInformation>
            </Abstract>
